cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "qb-compiler: preflight, cost and provenance checks for quantum circuit execution"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Michael William Perry
    family-names: Walshe
    affiliation: QubitBoost
    email: mike@qubitboost.io
repository-code: "https://github.com/mwpwalshe/qb-compiler"
url: "https://mwpwalshe.github.io/qb-compiler/"
abstract: >-
  qb-compiler is a preflight layer for quantum circuit execution. It reports whether a circuit is
  viable on a chosen backend, what it will cost across vendors, which physical qubits a
  calibration-aware layout search selected and how old the calibration behind that choice was, and
  whether a decoder input or a chemistry input is well formed before any shots are bought. Every
  check emits a machine-readable receipt that a third party can verify offline. It is a Qiskit
  Ecosystem member and uses Qiskit for transpilation and routing.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum compiler
  - qiskit
  - calibration
  - quantum error correction
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
